  "info": {
    "description": "API backend for **Twin2Clouds**, a cost-optimization platform for engineering digital twins across multiple cloud providers (AWS, Azure, Google). This API serves both the web UI and the computational engine that calculates the most cost-efficient provider setup for each architectural layer.<h3>\ud83d\udd17 Useful Links</h3><h4>\ud83d\udda5\ufe0f Web Interface</h4><ul><li><a href=\"/ui\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Open Web UI</strong></a></br>  The graphical Twin2Clouds interface for configuring scenarios.</li></ul><h4>\ud83d\udcd8 Documentation</h4><ul><li><a href=\"/documentation/docs-overview.html\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Documentation Overview</strong></a></li></ul>",
    "title": "twin2clouds REST API",
    "version": "1.2"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/calculate": {
      "put": {
        "description": "**Purpose:** Computes the most cost-effective distribution of Digital Twin services across AWS, Azure, and GCP based on your scenario parameters and the pinned thesis pricing catalogs.\n\n**When to use this endpoint:**\n- Before deploying a new Digital Twin to determine the cheapest provider configuration\n- When comparing costs across different scenario configurations\n- To understand cost breakdown by architectural layer\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Takes your Digital Twin parameters (device count, message frequency, storage needs, etc.)\n2. Resolves the exact reviewed provider-region catalogs supplied in `providerPricingCatalogs`\n3. Enumerates every executable assignment inside the Six-layer v1 profile\n4. Prices its reviewed direct, tiering, Twin-projection, and Cross-Cloud routes\n5. Scores complete layer and route totals and returns the deterministic winner\n6. Returns detailed cost, route, billing-pool, and immutable evidence context\n\n**The fixed Six-layer responsibilities:**\n- **L1 (Ingestion):** IoT data acquisition - receives telemetry from devices\n- **L2 (Processing):** Data processing, event detection, notifications\n- **L3 (Storage):** Hot/Cool/Archive storage tiers - each can be on different providers\n- **L4 (Management):** Digital Twin state and bounded relationship management\n- **L5 (Visualization):** Dashboards and user interfaces\n\n- **L6 (Eventing):** Independently assigned event routing between processing and consumers\n\n**Important:** This is a calculation-only endpoint. It does not deploy any resources. Use the Deployer API's `/infrastructure/deploy` to actually provision infrastructure.",
        "operationId": "calculateOptimalCloudDistribution",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SixLayerCalcParams"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "result": {
                    "calculationResult": {
                      "L1": "GCP",
                      "L2": "AWS",
                      "L3": {
                        "Archive": "AWS",
                        "Cool": "GCP",
                        "Hot": "AWS"
                      },
                      "L4": "Azure",
                      "L5": "Azure"
                    },
                    "cheapestPath": [
                      "L1_GCP",
                      "L2_AWS",
                      "L3_hot_AWS",
                      "L3_cool_GCP",
                      "L3_archive_AWS",
                      "L4_Azure",
                      "L5_Azure"
                    ],
                    "currency": "USD",
                    "optimizationDiagnostics": {
                      "enumeratedPathCount": 972,
                      "evaluatedPathCount": 972,
                      "rejectedPathCount": 0,
                      "schemaVersion": "complete-path-optimization.v1",
                      "scoreUnit": "USD/month",
                      "winningCandidateId": "gcp|aws|aws|gcp|aws|azure|azure"
                    },
                    "optimization_profile_id": "cost_minimization_v1",
                    "result_schema_version": "cost-result.v1",
                    "totalCost": 85.5,
                    "transferPricingContext": {
                      "currency": "USD",
                      "pools": [],
                      "routes": [],
                      "schemaVersion": "complete-path-transfer-pricing.v1"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "schema": {}
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful calculation - returns cost breakdown and optimal configuration"
